{"kind":"request","text":"Reduce the fixed cost of a one-base append to the separate 50 ms product target.","body":{"branch":"request/fixed-append-cost","conditions":"1. Begin implementation only after proposal 3db9488e is adopted and the active scale-document head is settled; route the work to an available implementer on a fresh request branch and do not amend head 18bbedf4. 2. Profile submit_ack with fan-out 1 and attribute time among signing, object creation, verified-ref sequencing, verification, fold and publication; keep setup outside the measured operation exactly as the harness does. 3. At the contract linear one-actor fixture, median end-to-end one-base submit_ack latency is at most 50 ms at PREVIEW depth 50,000 and FIRST-PRODUCTION depth 500,000, with at least seven alternating exact-head versus main rounds, raw retained evidence, named fixture/head/environment, ranges, and equal trusted/projected correctness digests. 4. Preserve actor and sequencer signatures, bounds, admission, verified-ref compare-and-swap, idempotency, complete fold semantics, error behavior and atomic publication; no deferred verification, reduced validation or stale projection may buy the result. 5. Add deterministic correctness and concurrency regressions for the optimized path, run the race detector on affected packages, and follow exact-head artifact, independent review, succession and merge discipline. 6. If the fixed 50 ms bound cannot be met without an architecture change, stop after a measured design proposal that names the irreducible stage and requests the narrower authority; do not weaken the bound silently.","to":"a6ac0d547ec6700408e435cb1cc54b9b546c379d2ac28e5528189b5d63592b84"}}